<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Durations the sub-pages need that `values/motion.xml` does not carry.

  A separate file for the same reason `motion_onboarding.xml` is one — `motion.xml`
  belongs to the foundation wave and is edited by everyone — and NOT a second motion
  scale. Everything already named there is used from there; only a number the handoff
  states outright and the foundation had no reason to know about lands here.
-->
<resources>

    <!--
      README §7 «Устройства»: «при удалении строка гаснет, подпись меняется на
      "Отключено от подписки", через 700 мс уходит из списка». 700 is the whole gesture
      — the dim, the held moment in which the new subtitle can be read, and the exit —
      not the length of any one of its parts.
    -->
    <integer name="motion_device_release">700</integer>

    <!--
      README §7, «Единое лекало»: «Появление — простое проявление 260 мс». The pair used
      to read @integer/motion_reveal 300 / motion_reveal_exit 225, which is the internal
      choreography table's number for a reveal in general — and 300 is also §4's shield
      crossfade, so retiming the shared token to satisfy §7 would have moved the connect
      object with it. A sub-page opening is its own role and gets its own two numbers.

      The exit stays 75% of the enter (00-rules.md 8.5), which is 195. The handoff does
      not state an exit; the ratio does, and the two files are a pair that is never
      retimed one at a time.
    -->
    <integer name="motion_subpage_enter">260</integer>
    <integer name="motion_subpage_exit">195</integer>

</resources>
